1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
Last time this room had a name.

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:06,102
Today it has something to say.

3
00:00:06,552 --> 00:00:13,509
I flew the ship into the Vault, and a recording forty years old started to play.

4
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:18,307
I did not write a line of code for that.

5
00:00:18,757 --> 00:00:25,713
I wrote who is speaking, what he says, and how close the ship has to be.

6
00:00:26,913 --> 00:00:31,696
A place in a ruin can speak to two different listeners.

7
00:00:32,146 --> 00:00:37,798
The ship, which means the bridge: that arrives on Comms as a call.

8
00:00:38,248 --> 00:00:48,248
Or a person, a crew member who has gone outside in a suit and is standing there: that is read on their handheld.

9
00:00:48,698 --> 00:00:50,437
They are written differently.

10
00:00:50,887 --> 00:00:55,235
And here is the thing to know before we start.

11
00:00:55,685 --> 00:01:00,033
Your crew does not leave the ship until Lecture 8.

12
00:01:00,483 --> 00:01:05,265
So today you will write both, and you will play one.

13
00:01:05,715 --> 00:01:10,063
The other one lint checks for you, and it waits.

14
00:01:11,263 --> 00:01:17,785
A call is placed by somebody, and a table of stone is not a somebody.

15
00:01:18,235 --> 00:01:21,278
So I give the place a voice.

16
00:01:21,728 --> 00:01:28,685
Forty years ago a survey team found this ruin, and their leader left recordings in it.

17
00:01:29,135 --> 00:01:34,787
He is a character, written the way you wrote characters in Class 2.

18
00:01:35,237 --> 00:01:36,976
His key is rook.

19
00:01:38,176 --> 00:01:39,480
Now the scene.

20
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:42,539
All of this is Class 2.

21
00:01:42,989 --> 00:01:44,293
Speaker: his key.

22
00:01:44,743 --> 00:01:49,091
When: hail, because this is a call that comes in.

23
00:01:49,541 --> 00:01:53,889
A title, which the crew reads before they open it.

24
00:01:54,339 --> 00:01:57,383
Two takes, and the game picks one.

25
00:01:57,833 --> 00:01:59,137
Then two answers.

26
00:01:59,587 --> 00:02:03,935
One leads on to a second scene, by its key.

27
00:02:04,385 --> 00:02:06,124
One ends the call.

28
00:02:06,574 --> 00:02:14,400
The second scene has no When and no title, because the only way into it is that answer.

29
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:20,817
A scene is words on a page until something places the call.

30
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:26,050
In Class 2 that was a beat waiting to be revealed.

31
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:30,413
This beat waits for the ship to get somewhere.

32
00:02:30,863 --> 00:02:35,211
Three hashes: it is not a step of First Contact.

33
00:02:35,661 --> 00:02:37,835
Beat on the first line.

34
00:02:38,285 --> 00:02:42,633
Then Starts when: reach altar 600. altar is a role.

35
00:02:43,083 --> 00:02:47,430
It is this word here, on the place's Roles line.

36
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:50,924
Not its key, and not its name.

37
00:02:51,374 --> 00:02:55,722
For the Altar they happen to be the same word.

38
00:02:56,172 --> 00:03:03,128
For the Way In they are not: the key is way_in and the role is entrance.

39
00:03:03,578 --> 00:03:06,187
And six hundred is how close.

40
00:03:06,637 --> 00:03:18,811
The Vault is seven hundred from the middle to the wall, and the altar is in the middle, so six hundred means the ship is in the room.

41
00:03:19,261 --> 00:03:21,000
Always write that number.

42
00:03:21,450 --> 00:03:28,407
Leave it out and the game uses five thousand, which is bigger than the whole ruin.

43
00:03:28,857 --> 00:03:34,509
Then Action, and under it who calls, the word hails, and the scene.

44
00:03:35,709 --> 00:03:42,230
You know what an answer can do: start a quest, finish one, send a word.

45
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:47,898
In a ruin there is one more. reveal, and then a place.

46
00:03:48,348 --> 00:03:52,261
Remember the Niche, the place I hid last time.

47
00:03:52,711 --> 00:03:58,363
It only showed up when the ship was nearly on top of it.

48
00:03:58,813 --> 00:04:03,161
With this answer it shows up when Comms says so.

49
00:04:03,611 --> 00:04:11,002
Now be careful: reveal takes the place's key, the word in round brackets. reach took its role.

50
00:04:11,452 --> 00:04:15,365
Two lines, two different words for the same place.

51
00:04:16,565 --> 00:04:18,304
Now the other listener.

52
00:04:18,754 --> 00:04:21,363
Somebody is standing at this table.

53
00:04:21,813 --> 00:04:23,552
Nobody is calling them.

54
00:04:24,002 --> 00:04:27,046
What they read is what they see.

55
00:04:27,496 --> 00:04:29,670
On the place, two lines.

56
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:33,163
Scene is the key of a scene.

57
00:04:33,613 --> 00:04:40,570
Scan is one line about the place, for whoever comes after the scene has been played.

58
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:44,498
And the scene itself: no fence at all.

59
00:04:44,948 --> 00:04:47,557
No speaker, because nobody is speaking.

60
00:04:48,007 --> 00:04:52,354
No When, no title, because it is not a call.

61
00:04:52,804 --> 00:04:55,848
Takes and answers, the same as ever.

62
00:04:56,298 --> 00:05:04,559
One rule is new: every path through a place's scene has to end in an answer with empty brackets.

63
00:05:05,009 --> 00:05:06,748
Nothing else closes it.

64
00:05:07,198 --> 00:05:11,111
This opens when a crew member's suit arrives here.

65
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,735
Not when the ship does.

66
00:05:14,185 --> 00:05:19,837
I cannot show it to you today, and you cannot play it today.

67
00:05:20,287 --> 00:05:23,765
We come back to it in Lecture 8.

68
00:05:24,965 --> 00:05:25,965
Lint. Clean.

69
00:05:26,415 --> 00:05:28,589
Now I break the role.

70
00:05:29,039 --> 00:05:34,257
It tells me nothing in the mission wears a role called alter.

71
00:05:34,707 --> 00:05:37,750
Good: that call would never have come.

72
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,504
Put it back.

73
00:05:39,954 --> 00:05:42,563
Now the scene on the place.

74
00:05:43,013 --> 00:05:48,665
It tells me the Altar points at a scene that is not there.

75
00:05:49,115 --> 00:05:53,463
That is how I check the half I cannot play.

76
00:05:53,913 --> 00:05:55,217
Put it back.

77
00:05:55,667 --> 00:05:58,276
Now the word after reveal. Clean.

78
00:05:58,726 --> 00:06:09,596
Lint does not check that word, and the game would say nothing either: the answer would end the call and the Niche would stay dark.

79
00:06:10,046 --> 00:06:18,741
So read two things yourself, every time: the word after reveal, and that there is a number after the role.

80
00:06:19,941 --> 00:06:22,550
In through the Mouth. The Nave.

81
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:29,957
Up the tunnel, and there is the Altar on the map, the same as last time.

82
00:06:30,407 --> 00:06:32,146
Now into the room.

83
00:06:32,596 --> 00:06:33,900
Comms: a call.

84
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:38,263
Surveyor Rook, a recording at the altar. Open it.

85
00:06:38,713 --> 00:06:40,887
One of my two takes.

86
00:06:41,337 --> 00:06:42,641
Play the rest.

87
00:06:43,091 --> 00:06:44,830
And: mark the Gallery.

88
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,585
Back to Helm.

89
00:06:47,035 --> 00:06:51,817
There is the Niche, and we have not been near it.

90
00:06:53,017 --> 00:06:58,670
Give the Niche a recording of its own, and words of its own.

91
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,728
Make one answer finish a quest.

92
00:07:02,178 --> 00:07:08,265
Then break one line where lint can see it and one where it cannot.

93
00:07:08,715 --> 00:07:12,193
Next time: what is lying in these rooms.
